# Multiline `) {` (not `){`)

Prefer a space between `)` and `{` on multiline method/constructor signatures:

```java
// ✅ GOOD
private String formatRegion(
        MessageRegion region,
        List<NamedRegion> namedRegions,
        int mergeDistance //
) {
```

```java
// ❌ BAD — formatter / style collapses to "){"
private String formatRegion(
        MessageRegion region,
        List<NamedRegion> namedRegions,
        int mergeDistance
){
```

## Why the trailing `//`

The autofomatter only keeps `) {` (space before `{`) when the **last parameter line** ends with an empty line comment `//`. Without it, formatting tends toward `){`.

## When to apply

- Multiline parameter lists (method, constructor, or similar declarations)
- Put ` //` at the end of the last parameter only — no text required after `//`
- Do not use this hack on single-line signatures; keep normal `) {` there
